<section class="review-section" id="faq">
<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"></line></svg> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>What types of threats does ZeroFox detect?</h4>
<p>ZeroFox detects phishing campaigns, brand impersonation, account takeovers, executive threats, data leakage, fraudulent domains, fake mobile apps, counterfeit products, trademark infringement, and social engineering attacks across digital channels.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>How quickly can ZeroFox take down malicious content?</h4>
<p>Takedown times vary by platform and threat type. Social media accounts are typically removed within hours, while domain takedowns may take 24-72 hours depending on registrar cooperation. ZeroFox achieves a 98%+ takedown success rate.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>Does ZeroFox integrate with existing security tools?</h4>
<p>Yes, ZeroFox integrates with major SIEM platforms (Splunk, QRadar, ArcSight), SOAR solutions (Phantom, Demisto), ticketing systems (ServiceNow, Jira), and threat intelligence platforms via REST API and native connectors.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>What platforms does ZeroFox monitor?</h4>
<p>ZeroFox monitors 4,000+ platforms including major social networks (Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn, Instagram), messaging apps, forums, app stores, domain registrations, paste sites, code repositories, dark web marketplaces, and underground forums.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>Is ZeroFox suitable for small businesses?</h4>
<p>While ZeroFox serves enterprises primarily, smaller organizations with significant digital presence or high-value brand protection needs can benefit. However, pricing and resource requirements may make it better suited for mid-size to large enterprises.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<h4>How does ZeroFox's AI work?</h4>
<p>ZeroFox employs machine learning models trained on billions of data points to classify threats, predict risk levels, identify patterns, and automate responses. Models continuously improve through feedback loops and expert analyst validation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="review-section" id="verdict">
<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 9H4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0-5H6"></path><path d="M18 9h1.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 0-5H18"></path><path d="M4 22h16"></path><path d="M10 14.66V17c0 .55-.47.98-.97 1.21C7.85 18.75 7 20.24 7 22"></path><path d="M14 14.66V17c0 .55.47.98.97 1.21C16.15 18.75 17 20.24 17 22"></path><path d="M18 2H6v7a6 6 0 0 0 12 0V2z"></path></svg> Final Verdict</h2>
<p>ZeroFox stands out as a premier digital risk protection platform that addresses the critical security gap beyond traditional perimeter defenses. Its comprehensive coverage of 4,000+ platforms, AI-powered automation, and proven takedown capabilities make it invaluable for organizations facing sophisticated external threats.</p>
<p>The platform excels in brand protection, executive security, and social media threat detection—areas where many traditional security tools provide limited visibility. The combination of automated detection and expert human analysis delivers both scale and accuracy, while rapid takedown workflows minimize exposure windows.</p>
<p>For enterprises with significant brand value, high-profile executives, or customer bases targeted by phishing and fraud, ZeroFox provides essential protection that justifies the investment. The platform's ability to detect and disrupt threats before they impact operations, reputation, or revenue has proven its value across financial services, retail, government, and other sectors.</p>
